# Unused Exports, Grouped by Kind

The same bound data as `unused-exports.stage`, presented a different way,
with no change to `unused-exports.js` at all: the script emits structured
data once, the document decides how to show it. `sort=`/`columns=` on
`@render` and `where=` on `@foreach` are the whole difference between the
two documents.

@code language="javascript" src="unused-exports.js" label="dead" visible="false" cache="persist" cache-key="../../src/**/*.ts" /

## Every dead export, sorted by kind rather than by file

@render source="dead.items" type="table" columns="kind,symbol,file" sort="kind" /

## Just the unused types

`where="kind == 'type'"` filters the same bound array before iterating,
no second script run:

@foreach item in {{ dead.items }} where="kind == 'type'"
- {{ item.symbol }} ({{ item.file }})
@foreach-end
